===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person engaged in various literary works: literary critic, {{l|en|essayist}}, {{l|en|writer}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1877|author=William Herman (pseudonym; {{w|Ambrose Bierce}})|title=The Dance of Death|pages=7–8|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/danceofdeath00bierrich#page/8/mode/1up|passage={{...}}; and fourthly—as is evident upon the face of these pages—he is no professed '''litterateur''', who can be starved by adverse criticism.}}
#* '''1969''', Victor Ernest Watts (translator), [[w:Boethius|Anicius Manlius Severinus Boëthius]] (author), ''The {{w|Consolation of Philosophy}}'', {{w|Penguin Books}}, book III, chapter v, page 88, footnote 4:
#*: Lucius Annaeus Seneca, the Roman philosopher, playwright and '''''littérateur''''', was the boyhood tutor of the emperor Nero, and later on his adviser.

